{"artifacts":[],"checksum":"sha256:60593239e8b0f8f15a7054ba7e2a6b75dd3bb5368b5adf42b054aded86681b37","events":[{"actor":{"id":"system-runtime","type":"system"},"artifactRefs":[],"eventHash":"sha256:8f9078a701ad25984067702af392be5f4e37d67ed7de325a2500955559f1ac39","eventId":"event-46184f30-556b-4687-8ed3-8b6fb888a75b","evidenceRefs":[{"ciphertextSha256":"0a5453e1cec94dd8a2dfd81d30185c367371a0b6bbd0d07a59a34915b2cfc0c4","contentSha256":"b2b9bcab215aad17993ef3ea8df8b2e69e19bdd9888cd6a0aad45082ffd6eaa5","evidenceId":"exec-exec-m08-judge5-judge-a1-judgment"}],"idempotencyKey":"node-outcome-2a59b378-c217-4ea9-aeaf-b8e7eebb2683","kind":{"data":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge5","nextState":"failed","nodeId":"judge","outcome":"terminal_failure","reason":"judge_refused"},"type":"node_outcome_recorded"},"occurredAt":"2026-08-18T20:15:26.467635600Z","previousHash":"sha256:e7f2b827c3071d043df3a2ab0b0a2e075ba2d9efabe870abfe0db2b55a0d6dc5","schemaVersion":"1.0.0","scope":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge5","projectId":"project-local","workspaceId":"workspace-local"},"sensitivity":"internal","sequence":15,"streamId":"exec-m08-judge5"},{"actor":{"id":"system-runtime","type":"system"},"artifactRefs":[],"eventHash":"sha256:e690b616c17337c12bc2dc8458ba2e1b68c2263603b3f3d0d39c5fbeb2f24113","eventId":"event-bc763edf-d913-4a30-b147-fbb7f9e82eb0","evidenceRefs":[],"idempotencyKey":"gate-verdict-a5945c8b-c567-4a39-aba8-29e74d8a25c7","kind":{"data":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge5","findings":[{"claim":"The one field that answers the story — `attention` in `status` — reads `\"unknown\"` with an empty `attentionReasons` array, both on first open and 60s later. The glance yields no go-back-to-sleep answer at all; the operator gets a null verdict rather than yes/no.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Make `attention` a total function over observable state (`ok` | `needs_operator` | `degraded`), never `unknown` for a live execution, and always populate `attentionReasons` with the concrete drivers (failed/queued-after-failure nodes, unevaluated silence budgets, untriaged interruptions).","severity":"critical"},{"claim":"`flaky_check` recorded `retryable_failure` / `tool_exited_non_zero` at 20:13:23 and sits in `queued`, but `status` shows `failed: 0`, no retry count, no last-failure field, and `attention: unknown`. A glancing operator sees `status: running` with a clean state histogram and concludes all is well while a node is actively failing.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Surface retryable failures in the summary: add `retriesInFlight` / `lastFailure` (node, reason, occurredAt, attempt) to `status`, and let any non-zero retry count drive `attention` off `ok`.","severity":"high"},{"claim":"`judge` has been `running` since 20:13:24 with zero events for 60+ seconds, and `silenceUnevaluated: [{node: judge, reason: no_declared_budget}]` means stall detection is switched off for exactly the node that is stuck. A hung node can therefore never raise attention, which is the failure mode the operator most needs to be woken for.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Apply a default silence budget when a node declares none, and treat `silenceUnevaluated` as a degraded-observability condition that itself sets `attention` to needs-operator with the node named.","severity":"high"},{"claim":"Nothing in `status` explains itself; discovering the flaky_check failure required paging the raw hash-chained event log and reading 13 envelopes of runtime bookkeeping. The 'one glance' costs at minimum a second call plus manual event triage.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Fold a human-readable digest into `status` (last N state-changing events with node, outcome, reason, timestamp) so no event-log read is needed to answer the sleep question.","severity":"medium"},{"claim":"Arming the wake lease appended `wake_lease` event seq 14 to the same stream, so `headSequence` advanced 13 → 14 while `lastEventAt` stayed at 20:13:24. Monitoring mutates the very counter an operator reads as a liveness proxy, and the two progress indicators now contradict each other.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Keep observer-side lease events out of the content stream (or expose `contentHead` — already computed internally — as the headline progress field) so operator instrumentation cannot fake forward motion.","severity":"medium"},{"claim":"`wake_wait` returned `{\"outcome\":\"timeout\"}` with no indication of whether the execution is still healthy, so the sanctioned block-and-wait path also ends with no answer and forces another full `status` + `events` round trip.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Include the attention verdict and content head in the wake_wait timeout reply, or document that a timeout means 'no change since armed cursor' so the operator can act on it directly.","severity":"low"}],"gateId":"judge-usefulness","nodeId":"judge","passed":false},"type":"gate_verdict"},"occurredAt":"2026-08-18T20:15:26.467635600Z","previousHash":"sha256:8f9078a701ad25984067702af392be5f4e37d67ed7de325a2500955559f1ac39","schemaVersion":"1.0.0","scope":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge5","projectId":"project-local","workspaceId":"workspace-local"},"sensitivity":"internal","sequence":16,"streamId":"exec-m08-judge5"}],"evidenceIds":["exec-exec-m08-judge5-judge-a1-judgment"],"expectedNextSequence":15,"formatVersion":"1.0.0","requestDigest":"sha256:aa5d485660fb5f9679172f7a9352b69ecf168a7dd5cbd951beab191c9c9ef179","scope":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge5","projectId":"project-local","workspaceId":"workspace-local"},"streamId":"exec-m08-judge5"}
